  "normalization": "Line-by-line reading transcription made on 2026-10-22 directly from the page images of the parent facsimile (Google public viewer images at 1600 px width), with the retained 575 px whole-book images as a cross-check; no OCR or modern edition controls any word. Greek is polytonic as printed: letters, acute/grave/circumflex (including printed graves before punctuation), breathings, diaeresis, capitalization and punctuation follow the page. Iota subscripts are encoded only where printed; datives printed without one are kept so. Greek ano teleia is encoded U+00B7 and elision U+2019. Typographic ligatures and suprascript abbreviations (for example the καί ligature, ου and ος ligatures, suprascript τοῦ/τῶν/τὸν/αὐτοῦ/αὐτὸν/μετὰ forms) are expanded to the full printed word; the δια ligature is expanded in lowercase. Spaced small-capital headings are encoded as Unicode capitals with their printed accents and breathings; institution words keep the case in which each edition prints them. A red initial letter beginning black text belongs to the black text. Running heads, page numbers, signatures, catchwords, ornaments, drop-cap sizing and line-end word division are removed; words broken across lines or pages are joined. Each printed block of a different class (red heading, red rubric, black reading text, footnote) starts a new line, and every block is broken mechanically after each . · : or ; followed by a space (an ellipsis is never broken). The extent record classifies each physical line. Encoding: NFC UTF-8, LF line ends, one final LF.",
